---
description: How to run or type-check TypeScript files in this repo
globs: ["**/*.ts"]
alwaysApply: true
---

Never run `tsc` directly on a single file (e.g. `tsc some/file.ts` or `npx tsc some/file.ts`).
Passing a filename to `tsc` on the command line makes it ignore `tsconfig.json` entirely
(including `noEmit: true`), which leaves stray `.js` / `.js.map` files next to the source.

- To run/execute a `.ts` file (server code): use `npx tsx path/to/file.ts`.
  The project already runs this way via `npm start` / `npm run start:dev`.
- To type-check without executing or emitting anything: use
  `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` (server code) or
  `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.client.json` (browser code under `static/`).
- Never invent ad-hoc `tsc` invocations to "quickly check" a file — use the commands above.
